{"book":23,"chapter":8,"context":{"chapter":8,"title":"Swift Plunder, Quiet Waters","summary":"Isaiah's newborn son is named Maher-shalal-hash-baz ('swift plunder') as a sign that Assyria will soon strip Damascus and Samaria. Because Judah rejects God's gentle waters, Assyria will flood it like a river; Isaiah is to fear God alone and wait for Him.","background":"Assyria did just this: it took Damascus in 732 BC and Samaria in 722 BC. 'The waters of Shiloah that go softly' (v. 6) were the gentle channel feeding Jerusalem's pool, a picture of the Lord's quiet care, set against 'the river,' the mighty Euphrates, standing for Assyria.","customs":[{"term":"Familiar spirits and wizards","verses":"8:19","note":"Mediums who claimed to consult the dead, forbidden by the Law (Deuteronomy 18:10-11). They 'peep and mutter,' imitating spirit voices."}],"watchFor":["'O Immanuel' (v. 8) and 'God is with us' (v. 10) are the same Hebrew words.","The Lord is both sanctuary and stumbling stone (v. 14), quoted in Romans 9:33 and 1 Peter 2:8.","'I and the children' (v. 18) is quoted in Hebrews 2:13."],"connections":["Deuteronomy 18:10-11","Romans 9:33","1 Peter 2:8","Hebrews 2:13"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיֹּאמֶר","vaiyomer","H559","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he said"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["אֵלַי","'elai","H413","HR/Sp1bs","to me"],["קַח","kach-","H3947","HVqv2ms","take"],["לְךָ","lekha","H9031","HR/Sp2ms","<for> yourself"],["גִּלָּיוֹן","gilayon","H1549","HNcmsa","a tablet"],["גָּדוֹל","gadol","H1419","HAamsa","large"],["וּכְתֹב","ukheto","H3789","HC/Vqv2ms","and write"],["עָלָיו","'alav","H5921","HR/Sp3ms","on it"],["בְּחֶרֶט","becheret","H2747","HR/Ncmsc","with a stylus of"],["אֱנוֹשׁ","'enoosh","H582","HNcmsa","a person"],["לְמַהֵר","lemaher","H4122","HR/Vpcc","<to> Maher-"],["שָׁלָל","shalal","H4122","HNcmsa","Shalal-"],["חָשׁ","chash","H4122","HVqrmsa","Hash-"],["בַּז","baz","H4122","HNcmsa","Baz"]],"x":[[23030008,23030008,7],[18019023,18019024,4],[23008003,23008003